[ ================================================================ ]
[ 030 -- variables                                                 ]
[                                                                  ]
[     phoenix examples/030_variables.phx                           ]
[ ================================================================ ]

[ `var` declares a variable and sets it to 0.                       ]
var x

[ `x !` takes the top of the stack and stores it into x.            ]
5 x !

[ Writing the name on its own pushes its value back.                ]
x print 10 printa

[ Expected output:                                                  ]
[                                                                   ]
[     5                                                             ]

[ The two together are the usual shape of an assignment: compute a  ]
[ value, then name where it goes.                                   ]
var y
x x * y !
y print 10 printa

[ Expected output:                                                  ]
[                                                                   ]
[     25                                                            ]

[ !! The `!` must come straight after a variable name. The target   ]
[ is worked out while compiling rather than taken off the stack, so ]
[ there has to be a name written there to work it out from. This is ]
[ a compile error:                                                  ]
[                                                                   ]
[     5 !                                                           ]
[     error: expected a variable name before `!`                    ]
[                                                                   ]
[ and so is this, because `var` already consumed the name:          ]
[                                                                   ]
[     var z !                                                       ]
[                                                                   ]
[ Write `var z  z !` instead.                                       ]

[ !! Declaring a name again resets it to 0 rather than making a     ]
[ second variable.                                                  ]
var x
x print 10 printa

[ Expected output:                                                  ]
[                                                                   ]
[     0                                                             ]

[ !! `var` is an instruction like any other, so it runs where it is ]
[ written. A variable declared inside a branch that is not taken    ]
[ does not exist, and using it is an error at run time rather than  ]
[ at compile time. Example 070 has more on this, once functions are ]
[ in the picture.                                                   ]
